(7481088, 1189696, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mefnj:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GeorgesBogaert:</b></div><hr/><i> Despite the typos, the presentation of your movie poster is great. Well done, and in my top 3. An 8 from me </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>ugh!... the "ie" vs. "ei" typo always gets me ... and i write A LOT for my job... thanks for the nice comment </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Cabaret</td>', 'Originally posted by mefnj: Originally posted by GeorgesBogaert: Despite the typos, the presentation of your movie poster is great. Well done, and in my top 3. An 8 from me   ugh!... the "ie" vs. "ei" typo always gets me ... and i write A LOT for my job... thanks for the nice comment   Cabaret', '2016-11-05 13:55:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481105, 1189742, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m a decent speller, but as with Beetle, I''m a careless reader. Didn''t notice misspellings. Didn''t score with any language penalties. What I like most here is the isolation of the subject, even in the context of a subway car. It really works for the title film title concept. Not sure I''d want to sit through it, though.</td>', 'I''m a decent speller, but as with Beetle, I''m a careless reader. Didn''t notice misspellings. Didn''t score with any language penalties. What I like most here is the isolation of the subject, even in the context of a subway car. It really works for the title film title concept. Not sure I''d want to sit through it, though.', '2016-11-05 18:26:46.000000', NULL, 0),
